---
title: Proposition 9
---
order: 9
---
short_label: VIII.9
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two numbers are relatively prime, and numbers fall between them in continued proportion, then, however many numbers fall between them in continued proportion, so many also fall between each of them and a unit in continued proportion.
----
proof:

Let *A* and *B* be two numbers relatively prime, and let *C* and *D* fall between them in continued proportion, and let the unit *E* be set out.

I say that, as many numbers fall between *A* and *B* in continued proportion as fall between either of the numbers *A* or *B* and the unit in continued proportion.

